Filename: org.webosarchive.tls-updates_1.0.18_all.ipk
Description: TLS 1.3 Updates - SSL/TLS, root certs, App Catalog, Help, USB, gamepad, Accounts and Backup fixes
Maintainer: webOS Archive
Source: { "Type":"OS Application", "Feed":"WOSA Modernize", "Category":"Modernize", "LastUpdated":"1787609034", "Title":" TLS 1.3 Updates (TouchPad)", "FullDescription":"One-tap bundle of the safe webOS Archive modernization patches. Pulls in: modern OpenSSL 1.1.1w + TLS 1.2/1.3 for the browser, command-line curl, in-app WebKit (Mojo/Enyo), the mail client and the system Download Manager; updated Mozilla root certificates; NTP clock sync (so TLS certificate validity windows pass and apps work); the mojomail IMAP tag fix; the Help app redirect to help.webosarchive.org; and the Enyo App Catalog.<br><br>It also pulls the community <b>Accounts</b> app (com.palm.app.accounts), which replaces the stock Accounts app and re-enables System account management -- sign in, profile, the devices on the account, sign out -- through the community account endpoint. It is the same build the webOS CE 3.1.0 release candidate ships, so the accounts list is captioned SYNERGY ACCOUNTS and is ready for the Synergy Revival connectors if you add them later.<br><br><b>If you already have Accounts (Community Build) installed, remove it first.</b> That package (org.webosarchive.accountsapp) came with this bundle up to 1.0.17 and is now retired: it replaces the same files and keeps its own saved copy of the original, so removing it after the new app is installed would quietly put the old Accounts app back. This bundle repairs both copies during install, so removing the retired package afterwards is safe -- but removing it first is cleaner.<br><br>Uninstalling the new Accounts app does not put HP's original back; the copy it replaced is kept as /media/cryptofs/core-apps-backup*.tar.<br><br>It also pulls <b>Backup and Restore</b>, which replaces the built-in Backup app -- that one has been dead since Palm's cloud servers went dark in 2013 -- with one that keeps backups on the device, in /media/internal/webos-backups, and can restore accounts, settings, application data and the applications themselves.<br><br>It also pulls two hardware-enablement packages that are not TLS fixes but are part of bringing the tablet up to date, both included by community request: <b>USB Settings</b> (USB host/OTG mode, high-power devices, USB storage mount/unmount, a live connected-device list and a USB reset -- for wired controllers, keyboards and flash drives) and <b>Bluetooth Gamepad Support</b> (pairs a DualShock 4 or other classic Bluetooth HID pad as a real gamepad). Between them, wired and wireless game controllers both work.<br><br>webOS 3.0.5 or higher (TouchPad) only. Does not install QupZilla, Atlas or LunaCE. The device reboots once at the end of the install.<br><br>Changelog:<br>1.0.18: replace the community Accounts app (org.webosarchive.accountsapp, now retired) with com.palm.app.accounts 3.1.1 -- the same app plus the SYNERGY ACCOUNTS grouping, the Delete Account Data page and the missing translations. If the retired package is still installed, uninstall it; this bundle makes that safe to do at any time.<br>1.0.17: require USB Settings 1.1.9 -- a mounted USB drive now appears at /media/usb, so it no longer shows up as an empty folder (with files copied into it going to internal storage instead of the stick) in Internalz Pro and other file managers.<br>1.0.16: require in-app TLS 1.1.4 -- a version-alignment build. On the TouchPad this changes only the wording of installer log messages; the functional fixes in 1.1.4 are for the webOS 2.x phones.<br>1.0.15: add Backup and Restore -- a working local backup/restore for the device, replacing the built-in app that has had nowhere to talk to since 2013.<br>1.0.14: require Download Manager TLS 1.3 1.1.0 -- fixes a crash that took the download service down roughly once every couple of dozen downloads, and repairs an uninstall restore point that could otherwise leave downloads dead.<br>1.0.13: add the community Accounts app -- replaces the stock Accounts app and re-enables System account management via the community endpoint.<br>1.0.12: require USB Settings 1.1.8 -- fixes a bug where the USB-monitor's controller check silently locked a gamepad away from any game launched afterward, and restores the 1.1.4 idle-daemon performance fix that a prior build had reverted.<br>1.0.11: require USB Settings 1.1.4 -- the idle USB-monitor daemon no longer forks a burst of processes once a second, fixing a game/frame-rate stutter it caused on some devices.<br>1.0.10: require USB Settings 1.1.0 -- auto-arms the OTG controller to fix a first-cable-insert hang, adds a live connected-device list, and adds a USB Reset button.<br>1.0.9: require USB Settings 1.0.8 -- high-power mode now also configures controllers the port left unconfigured.<br>1.0.8: add Bluetooth Gamepad Support to the bundle.<br>1.0.7: add USB Settings.<br>1.0.6: add the Download Manager TLS package.", "MinWebOSVersion":"3.0.5", "MaxWebOSVersion":"3.0.9", "PostInstallFlags":"RestartDevice", "PostUpdateFlags":"RestartDevice" }

