Maintainer: WebOS Ports <webos-ports@googlegroups.com>
Source: { "Type":"Application", "Feed":"WOSA Modernize", "Category":"Browser", "LastUpdated":"1787486400", "Title":"Atlas", "FullDescription":"Atlas is a modern WebKit browser for the HP TouchPad -- WPE WebKit 2.52 with TLS 1.3, HTML5 media, and current web-platform support, far beyond the stock 2011 browser. The device reboots once at the end of install to load the browser engine.<br><br>On webOS CE 3.1.0 nothing else is needed -- that build already carries the OpenSSL 1.1 stack Atlas links for HTTPS.<br><br>Version 0.9.11 fixes the browser engine freeze -- the hang after heavy pages or a few minutes of browsing, where nothing would load again until the engine was restarted -- at its source. It was never the GPU: three defects in the engine's own plumbing (the frame channel closing a socket WebKit already owned, frame acknowledgements piling up in a buffer nothing emptied, and a leftover debug hook deadlocking the JavaScript heap) are each fixed. On the same device the old engine froze after 8 page loads; the fixed one cleared 64 heavy page loads and a 12-minute animation soak. The Restart Browser Engine menu item stays as a backstop, but you should not need it.", "MinWebOSVersion":"3.1.0", "MaxWebOSVersion":"3.9.9", "PostInstallFlags":"RestartDevice", "PostUpdateFlags":"RestartDevice", "PostRemoveFlags":"RestartLuna", "Icon":"http://stacks.webosarchive.org/feeds/modernize/ipkgs/assets/icons/atlas.png" }

