Source: { "Type":"Application", "Feed":"WOSA Modernize", "Category":"Modernize", "Title":"Mojomail IMAP Tag Fix (Phones)", "FullDescription":"<b>webOS 2.2.4 phones only -- HP Pre 3 / HP Veer / Palm Pre 2.</b> Not for the TouchPad, which has its own build. One package covers all three phones: it selects the right binaries at install time from the device board name and refuses to patch a device it does not recognise. Requires webOS 2.2.4 -- an un-upgraded Veer (2.2.0) or Pre 2 (2.1.0) is not supported.<br><br>Optional, standalone one-byte patch of /usr/bin/mojomail-imap on webOS 2.2.4 phones (HP Pre 3 / HP Veer / Palm Pre 2): changes its hard-coded IMAP command tag prefix from ~A to AA. mojomail tags IMAP commands ~A1, ~A2, ...; some strict modern servers (e.g. Fastmail) reject a tilde in the tag with an untagged BAD response, which the stock client can never match to its request, so IMAP account validation hangs and fails (error 3099). AA1.. is accepted by every server. Independent of the TLS packages -- take it or leave it. md5-guarded to the stock binary, backed up to /var/luna, restored on removal. Useful together with org.webosinternals.mail-tls13 (which provides modern TLS for the mail transports).", "License":"Public Domain", "Icon":"http://stacks.webosarchive.org/feeds/modernize/ipkgs/assets/icons/mail.png", "LastUpdated":"1785207389", "MinWebOSVersion":"2.2.4", "MaxWebOSVersion":"2.9.9", "DeviceCompatibility":["Pre3", "Veer", "Pre2"] }

