Source: { "Type":"OS Application", "Feed":"WOSA Modernize", "Category":"Modernize", "LastUpdated":"1787587200", "Title":" TLS 1.3 Updates (Phones)", "FullDescription":"One-tap bundle of the modern TLS stack for <b>webOS 2.2.4 phones</b> -- HP Pre 3 (mantaray), HP Veer (broadway) and Palm Pre 2 (roadrunner). Pulls in: modern OpenSSL 1.1.1w + TLS 1.2/1.3 for the stock browser, command-line curl, in-app WebKit (Mojo/Enyo), the mail client and the system Download Manager; updated Mozilla root certificates; NTP clock sync (so TLS certificate validity windows pass); the mojomail IMAP tag fix; and the webOS 2.x HP App Catalog.<br><br>Each device-specific package here covers all three phones in one build and picks the right binaries at install time from the device board name, refusing to patch anything it does not recognise -- so the wrong build cannot be applied to the wrong phone.<br><br><b>Requires webOS 2.2.4.</b> An un-upgraded Veer (2.2.0) or Pre 2 (2.1.0) is not supported. Not for the TouchPad -- it has its own <i>TLS 1.3 Updates (TouchPad)</i> bundle. The device reboots once after install (required by the in-app TLS package).<br><br>Changelog:<br>1.0.1: require in-app TLS 1.1.4 -- PDK apps (<i>Linux binary</i> apps) now launch instead of failing silently at startup, and app installs and removals through Preware or WOSQI no longer wedge on a stuck IPKG lock.", "MinWebOSVersion":"2.2.4", "MaxWebOSVersion":"2.9.9", "DeviceCompatibility":["Pre3", "Veer", "Pre2"], "PostInstallFlags":"RestartDevice", "PostUpdateFlags":"RestartDevice" }

