Description: USB Settings - toggle USB host (OTG), high-power devices, and USB storage
Maintainer: webOS Archive
Source: { "Type":"Application", "Feed":"WOSA Modernize", "Category":"Modernize", "LastUpdated":"1787603201", "Title":"USB Settings", "FullDescription":"A Palm-style settings panel for the USB capabilities the TouchPad's OS hides.<br><br>Toggle <b>USB Host (OTG)</b> mode to use USB keyboards, game controllers and flash drives; enable <b>High-power devices</b> to run gear that draws more current than the port normally allows (such as a DualShock 4 over USB); and <b>mount / unmount USB storage</b> to browse a flash drive. Shows live status, a live list of connected devices (with icons for keyboard, mouse, gamepad and storage) while the panel is open, and posts a notification when a drive is detected, mounted or removed. A one-tap <b>USB Reset</b> recovers a device that stopped responding without a full reboot (refused while storage is mounted, so it can't yank a drive mid-use).<br><br>Self-contained: only uses capabilities and components already on the device, so it needs no other feeds. Adds no drivers, and there is no Bluetooth LE. Fully reversible.<br><br>Install <b>and uninstall via Preware / WebOS Quick Install</b>, then reboot. Do not use the launcher's Delete: it skips the cleanup script and would leave a background daemon running (the app hides its Delete button for this reason).<br><br>1.1.9: USB storage now mounts at <b>/media/usb</b> instead of a folder inside internal storage. Mounting under /media/internal made the drive look <i>empty</i> in Internalz Pro (and any file manager that reads the internal partition directly rather than through the mount table), and files copied into it silently went to internal storage instead of the stick. On a device whose root filesystem is still read-only, the old location is used as a fallback.<br>1.1.8: fixes a bug that made game controllers appear broken in OTHER apps -- the device monitor behind the \"input received\" indicator used to open each controller exclusively, silently starving every other reader, so a controller just verified here would then be dead in a game launched afterward. It now reads shared and never grabs, and releases as soon as the panel is no longer in front. Also restores the 1.1.4 daemon performance fix (builtins-only idle path) that an earlier build had inadvertently reverted.", "MinWebOSVersion":"3.0.0", "MaxWebOSVersion":"3.0.9", "PostInstallFlags":"RestartDevice", "PostUpdateFlags":"RestartDevice", "PostRemoveFlags":"RestartLuna", "License":"GPL", "Icon":"http://stacks.webosarchive.org/feeds/modernize/ipkgs/assets/icons/usbsettings-icon.png", "Screenshots":["http://stacks.webosarchive.org/feeds/modernize/ipkgs/assets/screenshots/usbsettings_screenshot.png"] }

