Description: Backup and Restore - local on-device backups, replacing Palm's dead cloud service
Maintainer: webOS Archive
Source: { "Type":"Application", "Feed":"WOSA Modernize", "Category":"Modernize", "LastUpdated":"1787448795", "Title":"Backup and Restore", "FullDescription":"<b>webOS 3.0.5 (TouchPad) only.</b> A working Backup and Restore, storing backups <b>on the device</b> instead of on Palm's servers.<br><br>The Backup app that ships on every webOS device still launches, but it cannot work: it was a thin UI over a service that uploaded everything to Palm's cloud, and those servers went dark in 2013. Nothing underneath is broken \u2014 every service that participates in backup still answers \u2014 so this replaces only the destination.<br><br><b>What it backs up:</b> accounts, contacts and calendar; system settings and preferences; browser data and stored credentials; application data; anything a third-party app registers for itself; and the applications themselves, reinstalled automatically on restore. Optionally your media from /media/internal, as individually selectable categories (off by default, since a local backup lives on the same volume).<br><br>Backups go to /media/internal/webos-backups as plain files you can copy off the device over USB. They are content-addressed, so an unchanged file is stored once no matter how many backups reference it.<br><br><b>Backups are not encrypted.</b> This is a deliberate departure from stock. The original encrypted every file with a device key that does not survive a webOS Doctor and does not exist on another device \u2014 making the backup unreadable in precisely the two situations you would reach for it. Anyone with access to the device's USB storage can read a backup, so move it somewhere safe if that matters to you.<br><br><b>Install with Preware or WebOS Quick Install, not palm-install, and reboot afterwards.</b> Only an install that runs the postinst as root can install the privileged helper the full backup needs, and move the dead built-in Backup app aside so this one wins the launcher tile; without that the app runs in a limited mode and says so. The built-in app is backed up and put back on uninstall.<br><br>This is built against webOS 3.0.5 specifically and is offered only to a device reporting exactly that version, because it has to move the built-in Backup app aside to win the launcher tile and that is not a thing to do against a build it was not tested on. Installing it another way (WebOS Quick Install, or ipkg by hand) bypasses that check, but the postinst applies the same rule itself: it reads /etc/palm-build-info and, on anything other than 3.0.5, installs the helper but leaves the built-in app alone \u2014 so the tile keeps opening the old, dead one.", "MinWebOSVersion":"3.0.5", "MaxWebOSVersion":"3.0.5", "PostInstallFlags":"RestartDevice", "PostUpdateFlags":"RestartDevice", "PostRemoveFlags":"RestartLuna", "License":"GPL v2 Open Source", "Homepage":"https://webosarchive.org", "Icon":"http://stacks.webosarchive.org/feeds/modernize/ipkgs/assets/icons/backup-icon.png" }

