Maintainer: webOS Archive
Source: { "Type":"OS Application", "Feed":"WOSA Modernize", "Category":"Synergy", "LastUpdated":"1787613000", "Title":" Synergy Revival Roll-up (Touchpad)", "FullDescription":"<b>This roll-up installation prepares your 3.0.5 Touchpad for Synergy Revival.</b><br><br><b>Experimental -- new in this feed.</b> Synergy Revival brings account-based messaging and cloud storage back to webOS: modern IM services (WhatsApp, Telegram, Signal, Teams, Discord, Google Chat, Facebook), cloud and photo storage (Dropbox, Google Drive, OneDrive, Box, MEGA, pCloud, Koofr, kDrive, HiDrive, Yandex Disk, S3, Flickr) and CalDAV/CardDAV -- all as real Synergy accounts under Settings &gt; Accounts, with contact linking and Messaging threads the way webOS always did it.<br><br><b>Before you install: remove the old Accounts app first.</b> If Preware lists <b>Accounts (Community Build)</b> (org.webosarchive.accountsapp) as installed -- it came with the TLS 1.3 Updates bundle up to 1.0.17 -- uninstall it BEFORE installing Synergy Revival. Synergy Revival ships a newer Accounts app that replaces the same files, and the old package keeps its own saved copy of the original: leave it installed and removing it later will quietly put the stock Accounts app back over the Synergy one, taking the SYNERGY ACCOUNTS section with it. If you forget, this package repairs both copies during install so the old one can then be removed safely.<br><br>This package is Part 1: the shared runtime (imlibpurple + the libpurple backend, the cloud core and the OAuth sign-in app) together with the updated Accounts, Contacts, Messaging and Phone apps and their frameworks and services. Install it first, then pick the connectors you want from the Synergy category -- every connector needs this bundle.<br><br>It also pulls <b>TLS 1.3 Updates</b> (the cloud connectors sign in over modern HTTPS through the system curl) and <b>Atlas</b> (the OAuth sign-in page is rendered by Atlas's browser engine -- the stock webview cannot complete a modern TLS handshake). Together that is a large download: budget roughly 130 MB before you add any connectors.<br><br>webOS 3.0.5 (TouchPad) only. webOS CE 3.1.0 already has Part 1 built in and does not need this package -- CE users install the connectors directly. Install through Preware, from this feed: WebOS Quick Install and a manual ipkg install skip the feed's device checks and the whole dependency chain. The device reboots once at the end of the install.<br><br>Uninstalling does not put the original HP apps back; the copies they replaced are kept as /media/cryptofs/core-apps-backup*.tar.<br><br><b>1.0.1:</b> the replacement Contacts and Messaging apps have been withdrawn. On a TouchPad those two are ipkg-managed apps rather than ROM directories, so installing over them removed the originals, and their installer then failed to put the replacements down -- leaving no Contacts or Messaging app at all. Everything else in Synergy Revival is unaffected. They will return once fixed upstream.", "MinWebOSVersion":"3.0.5", "MaxWebOSVersion":"3.0.9", "PostInstallFlags":"RestartDevice", "PostUpdateFlags":"RestartDevice", "PostRemoveFlags":"RestartLuna", "Icon":"http://stacks.webosarchive.org/feeds/modernize/ipkgs/assets/icons/synergy/synergy-rollup.png" }

